 "notes": "The man and the woman crouch cheek to cheek the whole clip and their heads overlap in almost every frame; the boxes are split along the line between the two faces, are mostly head-sized and lose parts (shoulders, arms, the oven gloves, whose owner is often unclear). Because both do the same things (watch the oven, smile, reach in) and the hands cannot be told apart, both get state phrases that fit only one of them (her head cloth, his beard). Man off at 4.0-5.0 (hidden behind her, only a bit of beard). Bread = the same loaf throughout: raw dough on the tray at 0.0-2.5, inside the lit oven 3.5-7.5, taken out 8.0-10.0; off at 3.0 (hidden by the door). 'a glove' = the oven glove; 'an oven' pill sits on the control panel / front. Couple, no single main person -> defaultVoice by evenId true = female.",
